cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "RF Drone Detector: passive RF drone detection with a YOLO detector trained on IQ-level synthetic spectrograms"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Jeonghwan
    affiliation: Independent researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/sinkei9456/rf-drone-detector"
license: AGPL-3.0
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
keywords:
  - drone detection
  - counter-UAS
  - RF signal detection
  - software-defined radio
  - HackRF
  - spectrogram
  - synthetic training data
  - YOLO
abstract: >-
  A HackRF One listens to 20 MHz of the 2.4 GHz band. Every 20 ms of IQ samples
  becomes a 640 x 640 spectrogram, and a YOLO26s detector, fine-tuned from COCO
  object-detection weights, draws boxes around drone video links, Wi-Fi and
  Bluetooth, giving the time and frequency of each drone signal. Training
  pictures are synthesized at the IQ level: pieces of real drone signals are
  added to real HackRF background noise, with crowded Wi-Fi and Bluetooth, drone
  signals weakened to the level measured at 30 m altitude, and signals cut by
  the 20 MHz receiver window. On real recordings never used for training, the
  released model found a DJI Neo 2 in 249 of 250 indoor pictures and in 350 of
  351 pictures at 30 m altitude where the signal is visible, and drew a drone
  box on 6 of 1,040 pictures without a drone. Re-running the full pipeline from
  the raw recordings in the original analysis environment gives the released
  weights exactly.
